With a_d = 1/log2(d): N0 = O(n log^2 n (log log n)^2) and the certified excess tends to beta(1);
so the full excess does not need width n^{5/3}; any a_d -> 0 with a_d >> 1/M gives N0 = n^{1+o(1)}.
